  "description": "The client intends to replace the existing roof covering due to its poor condition. The works will primarily involve replacing the current natural slate roof with natural Welsh slate tiles and carrying out any necessary repairs to the chimneys, soffits, and rainwater goods. The proposals are designed to retain the existing roof profile and overall appearance while ensuring long-term weatherproofing and durability. The project aims to balance the historic importance of the Grade II listing and conservation area with the need to improve durability, thermal performance, and weatherproofing, while preserving the original roof form and detailing. The existing roof is deteriorating, with slipped and damaged slates and evidence of water ingress, which threatens the structure and internal fabric. The replacement works will protect the building’s integrity, maintain its contribution to the Queensbridge Road Conservation Area, and ensure the roof continues to complement the building’s original character.",
